          ],
          "footnotes": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.096,
                0.559,
                0.901,
                0.598
              ],
              "content": "Remark : From the table above you can observe that as $\\angle \\mathrm { A }$ increases from $0 ^ { \\circ }$ to $9 0 ^ { \\circ }$ , sin A increases from 0 to 1 and cos A decreases from 1 to 0."
            },
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.146,
                0.604,
                0.9,
                0.624
              ],
              "content": "Let us illustrate the use of the values in the table above through some examples."
            }
          ],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_table_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.636,
            0.592,
            0.695
          ],
          "content": "**Example 6 :** In $\\Delta \\mathrm { A B C }$ , right-angled at B, $\\mathrm { A B }   =   5$ cm and $\\angle ACB = 30^{\\circ}$ (see Fig. 8.19). Determine the lengths of the sides BC and AC."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.7,
            0.594,
            0.778
          ],
          "content": "**Solution :** To find the length of the side BC, we will choose the trigonometric ratio involving BC and the given side AB. Since BC is the side adjacent to angle C and AB is the side opposite to angle C, therefore"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.612,
            0.641,
            0.899,
            0.752
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.707,
                0.758,
                0.806,
                0.777
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 8.19"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_image_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.368,
            0.785,
            0.501,
            0.827
          ],
          "content": "{ \\frac { \\mathrm { A B } } { \\mathrm { B C } } } = \\tan \\mathrm { C }",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.847,
            0.14,
            0.865
          ],
          "content": "i.e.,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.37,
            0.833,
            0.575,
            0.875
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{5}{BC} = \\tan 30^{\\circ} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.881,
            0.217,
            0.901
          ],
          "content": "which gives"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.377,
            0.878,
            0.53,
            0.902
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm{BC} = 5\\sqrt{3}    cm",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_14.jpg"
        },
